id: pm-rf120g
title: "Disposition the test-only escape hatch published through the ./cli entrypoint: 86 internal functions are consumer-visible API with no support intent"
description: "src/cli/main.ts exports _testOnly, an object of 86 internal helpers, and package.json publishes ./cli with dist/cli/main.d.ts. Consumers can import and type-check against every one of them. The SDK side already treats this as a governed decision: _testOnlyCliContracts carries a named exclusion reason. The ./cli side has never been dispositioned."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:cli","area:sdk",hygiene,surface
created_at: "2026-08-16T10:06:33.911Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T10:06:33.911Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: The published ./cli declaration either stops exposing _testOnly or the exposure carries a recorded reason in the surface snapshot's exclusion vocabulary; pm's own tests continue to reach the helpers through source imports rather than the package export; The chosen disposition is written into docs/SDK.md next to the executable_entry classification; A change to the set of exposed helpers is a classified surface change either way
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: The published CLI entrypoint exposes only what the project intends to support.
actual_result: "It exposes runPmCli plus 86 unsupported internal helpers, typed and resolvable by any consumer."
